 "doc": "Push to talk's key rules, one file byte-identical in the desktop and web repos (launch-gate 2026-11-07). hold + mic (2026-11-13, BRB privacy): a key press while I am away (BRB) never opens the mic and going away ends a hold; with push to talk on the mic is muted unless the key is held and I am not away; with it off the mute button decides (BRB mutes through it, and a person who unmutes by hand while away owns that). tail (P15, 2026-11-13): a release keeps the mic open tailMs more so the last word isn't cut (a press in that time continues the hold); while away (BRB) the release is immediate. pressExact (4-1, 2026-11-14): a press starts a hold only when no OTHER modifier is held (Shift+F10 with an F10 key is the menu key, not push to talk; Shift+Ctrl with a Ctrl key is a chord) and nothing handled the press already (web: defaultPrevented; the desktop's shortcuts take their key before any press), then the press rule above. pressPopup (4-2): while a dialog, menu or other popup owns the keyboard focus no press starts a hold (with Ctrl as the key, a Ctrl in the \"Send as text?\" dialog or a keyboard menu transmitted); otherwise the pressExact rule.",
